// The scope one name keeps one type in. Every unit of the program -- its own
// tree and each tree it imports -- is one scope, and the standard library's
// units are the other: a library's internals are checked against each other by
// the library's own build, and against the program by std_var_pass
// (../ext/check/pass/var/), which reports at the program's declaration. A build
// with no library (`stdunit` -1) has the one scope.

unit_scope(int unit) {
  int scope = 0;
  if((import stdunit)[0] >= 0 && unit >= (import stdunit)[0]) {
    scope = (import stdunit)[0];
  }
} return int scope;
given regrow_d (3):(0)
given regrow_d given integer_list_set((import stdunit), 0, 2) (3):(2)
given regrow_d given integer_list_set((import stdunit), 0, 2) (1):(0)
